<section class="relative py-20 sm:py-28 lg:py-32 bg-background">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      {/* Eyebrow */}
      <div class="mb-8">
        <span class="inline-block text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">
          The Foundation of Structured Engineering
        </span>
      </div>

      {/* Heading */}
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-8 leading-tight">
        Complex systems. One common language.
      </h1>

      {/* Content */}
      <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Modern engineering projects involve thousands of interconnected systems, components, and
          disciplines. Without a shared structure, information becomes fragmented, communication breaks
          down, and complexity becomes difficult to manage.
        </p>

        <p class="text-foreground font-medium">
          <strong>ISO/IEC 81346 provides a common framework for structuring, classifying, and identifying
          technical systems.</strong>
          It establishes a consistent language that connects people, processes, and information — from initial
          design to operation and maintenance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
